n/f939dbf9ac60b3bb68fae785b704e995bea0bf29f57322c65884ecf0fe435db4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130951" :question/id #uuid "d08fdd6f-e7ad-5c58-bb46-64ef9f075371" :question/math-academy-id "q-130951" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $R$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $R$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns:\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $4$th column." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130951/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f0d2e9-1cf6-5fe4-85cc-f401382f39b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130951"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130953/selection/7ecc4f7ccd7b31c52ec667b9451c3a652c6686232f19b378cdcbd5141e414a2b" :answer/id #uuid "6bb0ec5a-6781-5d33-9e7b-73e42215938b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd and $5$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130953/selection/f939dbf9ac60b3bb68fae785b704e995bea0bf29f57322c65884ecf0fe435db4" :answer/id #uuid "2f74ad50-7430-5dbc-84ac-d80c7e1bcc93" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130953/selection/a3ee0c4aa9937771ecbfc759c308f6bf5d7feef8a761401b24c3e7f601ed4d01" :answer/id #uuid "ee04422b-9124-56c2-9b98-4a81d3395c57" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130953/selection/4e225c83a94733e7a7d917657022ddd65fcd16a0d915ea05a2159a6162b187f0" :answer/id #uuid "287b38ee-41c7-5532-a8a3-471340d91