\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 4 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0 & 20 & -35 & 24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 4 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-35452/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1073953e-7e0a-5237-8533-8882b7772741"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35452"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73639/selection/061f9ca714dda64757af5802f2d3acf55e9f582e5c8fd8a9311baf5fc8130996" :answer/id #uuid "8994bccd-6d52-57c1-92b8-07767033862a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, $5$th, and $6$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73639/selection/c9bd598483f0e4ffa4aff63b848670ed0a8116c93b6b90c3356508f7f359ebeb" :answer/id #uuid "9a6854e2-1d02-5f7c-8a64-a4d6a08626c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd, $3$rd, and $6$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73639/selection/190f390d5ec4a51352cb3fc0ff84970da08590ea40fe2b735969db9829be788f" :answer/id #uuid "2aaac75f-1f8e-5164-af40-e26c891ddf01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd, $3$rd, $5$th, and $6$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73639/selection/de48298d0934fbaf1f791e7ef557fb148b38b70e2e88cb84e0d26f454a5c6b20" :answer/id #uuid "adfdbd7d-dc98-5b98-947c-8fa72fd49648" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st and $6$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73639/selection/f939dbf9ac60b3bb68fae785b704e995bea0bf29f57322c65884ecf0fe435db4" :answer/id #uuid "4e370edd-bf0a-5c8c-bfa7-174eccfbf0d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73639/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b9f91e3-60cd-5372-a09a-1178154a4263" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73639/selection/190f390d5ec4a51352cb3fc0ff84970da08590ea40fe2b735969db9829be788f" :answer-field/choices ["q-73639/selection/061f9ca714dda64757af5802f2d3acf55e9f582e5c8fd8a9311baf5fc8130996" "q-73639/selection/c9bd598483f0e4ffa4aff63b848670ed0a8116c93b6b90c3356508f7f359ebeb" "q-73639/selection/190f390d5ec4a51352cb3fc0ff84970da08590ea40fe2b735969db9829be788f" "q-73639/selection/de48298d0934fbaf1f791e7ef557fb148b38b70e2e88cb84e0d26f454a5c6b20" "q-73639/selection/f939dbf9ac60b3bb68fae785b704e995bea0bf29f57322c65884ecf0fe435db4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73639" :question/id #uuid "f2052ae3-18ce-5501-8a06-ca8f9c529ebd" :question/math-academy-id "q-73639" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 0 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 0 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $2$nd, $3$rd, $5$th and $6$th columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73639/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73639"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131302/selection/992b3a8fa4f7bb044b26fbfe2969c083530fd0149cebc8991c72d70a1f42d68f" :answer/id #uuid "e9f2567e-7e0a-51e7-b569-d3490577a2fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131302/selection/eeb4d250eb178da53234cb863d7d7469d2bab9f37bb1bcec382bcd3c0eb032eb" :answer/id #uuid "22ab3d8a-d8dc-57c6-91d3-ac3029c4b113" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131302/selection/02b0be138d8a0f39c7c3b7759031408a6993e6def8ee036ed0124e8b802e1efa" :answer/id #uuid "feaf37d9-9ed3-5ee2-8818-b14b8ccbbd56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st and $2$nd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131302/selection/3285ac7a1ec3e37cff711754ff5b9f24b211cdc7bdcb2feea0a837f447671434" :answer/id #uuid "535afafc-e10d-5eb2-bc92-5dd77118c720" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131302/selection/4e225c83a94733e7a7d917657022ddd65fcd16a0d915ea05a2159a6162b187f0" :answer/id #uuid "682a828a-6a0c-5f67-939e-a2de891109d5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131302/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "38011b36-bee0-5e04-9171-235eeb9ff009" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131302/selection/eeb4d250eb178da53234cb863d7d7469d2bab9f37bb1bcec382bcd3c0eb032eb" :answer-field/choices ["q-131302/selection/992b3a8fa4f7bb044b26fbfe2969c083530fd0149cebc8991c72d70a1f42d68f" "q-131302/selection/eeb4d250eb178da53234cb863d7d7469d2bab9f37bb1bcec382bcd3c0eb032eb" "q-131302/selection/02b0be138d8a0f39c7c3b7759031408a6993e6def8ee036ed0124e8b802e1efa" "q-131302/selection/3285ac7a1ec3e37cff711754ff5b9f24b211cdc7bdcb2feea0a837f447671434" "q-131302/selection/4e225c83a94733e7a7d917657022ddd65fcd16a0d915ea05a2159a6162b187f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131302" :question/id #uuid "190c1f09-7ea5-53d8-a079-57d65ed02079" :question/math-academy-id "q-131302" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & ↔{R}_{4} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-131302/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131302"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131301/selection/c12325f74ab3486398192a8d5229dcc8858f296945874fe16d6865db6a7dc4f8" :answer/id #uuid "26fff076-4148-582e-9e58-d21f0251c11c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131301/selection/8c7626a29cdcabf55a88b5acac41dc4d33e615263d9fdae2a8d71b72a7ac7342" :answer/id #uuid "5967f473-e5aa-582e-be38-5fa9450d173b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$rd and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131301/selection/06bf89e9fe9bd2978d91ae6a9925dcc52276fdd44f8de901ef2103c38fcbff28" :answer/id #uuid "e8c4e550-4726-5909-9915-cd1c9e6bba0b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st and $3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131301/selection/992b3a8fa4f7bb044b26fbfe2969c083530fd0149cebc8991c72d70a1f42d68f" :answer/id #uuid "7fca8c2d-10fa-57bc-bc05-04c463a51050" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131301/selection/4e225c83a94733e7a7d917657022ddd65fcd16a0d915ea05a2159a6162b187f0" :answer/id #uuid "6b30a0d7-4dfd-54ff-8ded-a3f00f6f2b21" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131301/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae1a8fab-dfce-59c1-ab71-b5dbfd97f51c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131301/selection/4e225c83a94733e7a7d917657022ddd65fcd16a0d915ea05a2159a6162b187f0" :answer-field/choices ["q-131301/selection/c12325f74ab3486398192a8d5229dcc8858f296945874fe16d6865db6a7dc4f8" "q-131301/selection/8c7626a29cdcabf55a88b5acac41dc4d33e615263d9fdae2a8d71b72a7ac7342" "q-131301/selection/06bf89e9fe9bd2978d91ae6a9925dcc52276fdd44f8de901ef2103c38fcbff28" "q-131301/selection/992b3a8fa4f7bb044b26fbfe2969c083530fd0149cebc8991c72d70a1f42d68f" "q-131301/selection/4e225c83a94733e7a7d917657022ddd65fcd16a0d915ea05a2159a6162b187f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131301" :question/id #uuid "4886d83c-b3ad-5f5e-806e-c8853df57419" :question/math-academy-id "q-131301" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-131301/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131301"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35732"] :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{4} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35734"] :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4703"] :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its pivot columns?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4704"] :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $C$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $C$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4705"] :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4706"] :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{2}{7}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
